  "result": "Perfect! All 83 tests pass (69 from before + 14 new tests).\n\n## Summary\n\nCreated the render module for plain-text invoice output:\n\n**src/render.js** \u2014 `renderInvoiceText(invoice)`\n- Returns a plain-text invoice as a multi-line string\n- Line 1: Invoice number (e.g., \"INV-2025-0001\") or \"DRAFT\" if not issued\n- Line 2: Customer name (looked up from the customer database)\n- Lines 3+: One line per invoice item in format: `qty x name @ unitPrice = lineTotal`\n- Last line: `Total: <formatted total>`\n- All monetary amounts formatted using `formatEuros()` with currency symbol, thousand separators, and exactly 2 decimal places\n- Handles unknown customers gracefully with placeholder\n- Example output:\n  ```\n  INV-2025-0001\n  Northwind Studio\n  10 x Development (hour) @ \u20ac95.00 = \u20ac950.00\n  5 x Sticker sheet @ \u20ac0.50 = \u20ac2.50\n  Total: \u20ac952.50\n  ```\n\n**Test coverage** \u2014 14 new tests covering:\n- Draft vs issued invoice display\n- Customer name inclusion (including special characters)\n- Line item formatting (qty, name, unitPrice, lineTotal)\n- Thousand separator formatting for large amounts\n- Order preservation of lines\n- Multi-line and single-line invoices\n- Complete workflow (create \u2192 modify \u2192 issue \u2192 render)\n- Output printability and structure\n\nAll monetary amounts use `formatEuros()` consistently, ensuring human-readable formatting with proper currency symbols and separators throughout the rendering layer.",
